---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import SupportArticle from "../../components/infopages/SupportArticle.astro";
---
<BaseLayout>
  <SupportArticle path="/support/find-a-product" title="Find a product by name" intro="BeautyMark knows tens of thousands of products from Sephora, Ulta, Target, Soko Glam and lots of brands' own shops. Type a few words and pick yours. 🔍">

    <h2>Find a product</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Tap <strong>+</strong>, then <strong>Skip</strong> on the scan screen. (Or scan first, and come back to this if the scan doesn't find it.)</li>
      <li>On <strong>Add Product</strong>, tap <strong>Brand</strong> or <strong>Product name</strong>. The <strong>Find your product</strong> screen opens.</li>
      <li>Type words from the brand and the product name together, in any order. Partial words work: "cerave moist", "snail essence" and "rare blush" all find what you'd expect.</li>
      <li>Tap your product under <strong>Products</strong>.</li>
    </ol>
    <p> BeautyMark fills in the brand, name, shade, category and the store's link, and adds the product's photo. If you've already added a photo of your own, it keeps yours.
    </p>

    <h2>Browse one brand</h2>
    <p> Under <strong>Brands</strong>, tap a brand (it shows how many products we know for it). The screen changes to <strong>Choose a product</strong> and only searches that brand. Type part of the name to narrow it down.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Done</strong> (the ✓ on iOS 26 and later) keeps just the brand, if you'd rather type the name yourself.</li>
      <li><strong>All brands</strong> goes back to searching everything.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Already filled in the brand? Tapping <strong>Product name</strong> starts with that brand's products.</p>

    <h2>When your product isn't listed</h2>
    <p> The top row always offers <strong>Use "…"</strong> with exactly what you typed. Tap it (or the <strong>done</strong> key on the keyboard) to use your own words. New and niche products, minis, and sets might not be in our list yet.
    </p>

    <h2>Add a photo</h2>
    <p> Every product needs a photo. If the one from the list isn't right, or you typed the product in yourself, tap <strong>Add Photo</strong> at the top of Add Product and choose:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Camera</strong>: take a picture of your own.</li>
      <li><strong>Photo library</strong>: use a picture you already have.</li>
      <li><strong>Search on web</strong>: look up the product's picture online (available once a brand or name is filled in).</li>
    </ul>
    <p>A photo you take or choose yourself is never swapped out automatically.</p>

    <h2>Changing a product you already saved</h2>
    <p> Open the product, tap the <strong>•••</strong> button at the top right, then <strong>Edit</strong>. Tapping <strong>Product name</strong> opens the same search, starting with the name it has now, so you can add a word or pick a different product.
    </p>
  </SupportArticle>
</BaseLayout>
